    <panel_attributes>Additional constraints features
--

- A project member cannot be added more than once to the
same project.

- Once a project is published, it cannot be updated in 
any way. This includes its attributes, its members, 
and its associated components (inventions, campaigns, and strategies).

- If a manager add a member to a project, you can´t go back to
the past. That means that you can´t edit or delete the
member.

- kickOffMoment/closeOutMoment must be a valid time interval
in future wrt. the moment when a proyect is published.

- If a project is published, inventors, spokes people 
and foundraisers can not add their composites to that
project. 

- If a project is published, the manager can not 
add any new inventor, spoke person or fundraiser. 

- A project can not be deleted.

- Projects cannot be published unless they have
at least one invention

- Publishing a project implies that its components
(inventions, campaigns and strategies) must be 
published automatically, so their atributes 
startMoment and endMoment, must be inside the range
of kickOffMoment and closeOutMoment

kickOffMoment &lt;= MIN(startMoment de componentes)
closeOutMoment &gt;= MAX(endMoment de componentes)

- Publishing a project implies that its components
(inventions, campaigns and strategies) must be 
published automatically, so the system must check if 
each project components (inventions, campaigns
and strategies) have one or more components vinculated
(part | milestone | tactic)

- A sponsor could attach a sponsorship to a project 
only if the sponsorship and the project are 
published, and the startMoment of the sponsorship 
must be equal or after the momentOfPublication of the project

sponsorship.startMoment &gt;= project.momentOfPublication

- An audit could attach an audit report to a project 
only if the audit report and the project are 
published, and the startMoment of the audit report
must be equal or after the momentOfPublication of the project

audit.startMoment &gt;= project.closeOutMoment

bg=RED
layer=0</panel_attributes>
