      <h>440</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Additional constraints Dashboard
--

- numberOfProjectsManaged is the total number of projects that 
the Manager manage

- deviationOfProjectsManaged is the  difference between 
numberOfProjectsManaged with respect to the average number
of projects managed by the other managers (OTHER).

if there is only 1 manager that attribute is NA.

Calculation: A - B, where A is the number of projects of 
the current manager and B is the average of the others.
Using the absolute value ensures the deviation is always a
positive magnitude.

- minimumEffort is the lowest effort value recorded among 
the set of projects belonging to a manager.

- maximumEffort is the highest effort value recorded among
the set of projects belonging to a manager.

- averageEffort is the arithmetic mean of the effort scores 
across all projects managed by a specific manager

- deviationEffort is the standard deviation of the effort
values across all projects managed by a single manager.

Calculation: It is calculated using the square root of the 
variance (the average of the squared differences of 
the projects efforts from the mean (the mean of the 
projects efforts)



bg=RED

layer=0</panel_attributes>
